sbmk - minimal SlackBuild helper

sbmk is a small shell script for fetching and building individual
SlackBuilds.org packages using a temporary workspace under /tmp.

It is intended as a convenience tool, not a package manager.

sbmk uses the existing SlackBuilds.org metadata and runs SlackBuild
scripts unmodified, in the same way a user would do manually.


Design characteristics:

- uses SLACKBUILDS.TXT as a simple index
- fetches only the requested SlackBuild
- downloads source archives listed in the .info file
- does not resolve dependencies
- does not install packages
- keeps no local database or persistent state


Usage:

  sbmk PACKAGE
  sbmk PACKAGE --deps
  sbmk PACKAGE --keep

sbmk must be run as root, as required by SlackBuilds.


Relation to sbotools:

sbotools provides a complete SlackBuilds.org management workflow,
including dependency handling, queues, upgrades, and state tracking.

sbmk does not attempt to replace or replicate this functionality.

Its purpose is deliberately narrower: to provide a small, transparent
helper for users who prefer to manage dependencies and installations
themselves.

The difference is intentional.
